{"name":"Canvas Sneaker","hex":"#f6ebd3","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"canvas","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of coarse cloth, woven from hemp (traditionally) or from cotton and polyesters, useful for making sails, tents, and overcoats or as a surface for paintings.","A piece of such cloth stretched across a frame on which one may paint an artwork."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover (an area or object) with canvas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/canvas"},{"term":"sneaker","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who sneaks.","An athletic shoe with a soft, rubber sole. A trainer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sneaker"}],"entries":[{"title":"Canvas","blocks":[{"text":"Canvas is a durable plain-woven fabric used for making sails, tents, marquees, backpacks, shelters, as a support for oil painting and for other items for which sturdiness is required, as well as in such fashion objects as handbags, electronic device cases, and shoes. It is popularly used by artists as a painting surface, typically stretched across a wooden frame."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Sj%C3%B6manss%C3%A4ck_-_1991.jpg/330px-Sj%C3%B6manss%C3%A4ck_-_1991.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canvas","wikidata":"Q4259259"},{"title":"Sneakers","blocks":[{"text":"Sneakers (US) or trainers (UK), also known by a wide variety of other names, are shoes primarily designed for sports or other forms of physical exercise, but are also widely used for everyday casual wear."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Air_Jordan_1_Banned.jpg/330px-Air_Jordan_1_Banned.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sneakers","wikidata":"Q1929383"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/